Subject to the conditions of this license, the Licensor grants you a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, copy, modify, merge and
distribute the Software and Derivative Works, and to create, use, publish and
distribute Output for any purpose, personal or commercial.


3. Branding of Output

(a) Every Output must open with the unmodified Intro, exactly as the Software
    produces it. You may not remove, shorten, replace, obscure, re-time,
    re-colour or otherwise alter the Intro, its mark, its name or its music.

(b) The name "narratr" must remain visible in the Intro of every Output.

(c) This condition applies to the Software and to every Derivative Work. It
    continues to apply if the Software is forked, cloned, copied or modified,
    including where the code that produces the Intro has been changed or
    removed. Changing the code does not release Output from this condition.

(d) Editing Output after it is produced (trimming, re-encoding, cutting it
    into other material) is permitted, provided the Intro stays intact at the
    start of the narratr-produced portion.


4. Attribution and credit

(a) You must keep this license and the copyright notice above in every copy
    of the Software and every Derivative Work, and include them with any
    distribution of either.

(b) Any Derivative Work, and any public description of it (a README, a
    website, a store listing, a paper, a talk), must state clearly that it is
    based on narratr, created by Aman Khandelwal, and link to
    https://github.com/amankhandelwal/narratr.

(c) You may not present the Software, the skill, its method of turning a
    document into a narrated video, or any Derivative Work as your own
    original creation, nor imply that you, rather than the Licensor, created
    them.

(d) You may not use the narratr name or mark to imply that the Licensor
    endorses you, your Derivative Work or your Output, except as required by
    Section 3.


5. Free forever

(a) The Software and every Derivative Work must be made available to its
    users free of charge. Commercial Distribution is not permitted.

(b) Any Derivative Work you distribute must be distributed under this same
    license, with its source code available, so that the people who receive
    it get the same freedoms and the same obligations.

(c) This Section restricts charging for the software. It does not restrict
    Output: videos made with narratr may be published, monetised and used
    commercially, provided they carry the Intro under Section 3.


6. Termination

If you breach any condition of this license, your rights under it end
automatically. They are restored if you cure the breach within 30 days of
becoming aware of it, unless you have breached this license before. Output
you distributed while in breach is not licensed.


